IMPORT prelude

-- Row il-68, TARGETED: the Families of Soldiers Killed in Action (Benefits and Rehabilitation) Law, 5710-1950. Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records three citations and amending instructions (I1, I2, I3) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the family member of a fallen soldier, the individual to whom the Law applies. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: the record of one reference with its two limbs, and the typed values each item needs. No reference is stated here; they are in fk68-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Two limbs are kept beside every reference, because a citation can be broken in two ways at once and a reader needs to know which part of the claim was read from what:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument that touched them.
-- Section numbers are written with Latin letters for the Hebrew ones the Law uses: 1C is 1 gimel, 9C 9 gimel, 9D 9 dalet, 13B 13 bet, 29A 29 alef, 29C 29 gimel;
-- a subsection letter (a) is alef, (b) bet, (c) gimel. The kinds and the plain descriptions below are this row's, not the Law's.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `read from an official instrument`
    `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `read from an official instrument; whether a later instrument touched the words was not read`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

DECLARE `A recorded reference` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing place` IS A STRING
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- I1: a citation of a subsection letter, and the section as the instrument prints it
DECLARE `A section as an instrument prints it` HAS
    `the section` IS A STRING
    `its subsection letters` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `printed by` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A citation of a section` HAS
    `the citing place` IS A STRING
    `the section the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the subsection letter the citing words name` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `Amendment 19 replaced the citing words` IS A BOOLEAN
    `printed by` IS A STRING

-- I2: a list of provisions, and a sentence that points at the section holding it
DECLARE `A list of provisions` HAS
    `printed by` IS A STRING
    `the provisions named` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `A pointer sentence` HAS
    `the citing place` IS A STRING
    `the section the sentence names` IS A STRING
    `printed by` IS A STRING

-- I3: a percentage, where it is printed, and whether it is text the Knesset printed for the provision
DECLARE `A percentage the pages print` HAS
    `the percentage` IS A NUMBER
    `printed in` IS A STRING
    `the text printed by the Knesset for the provision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `A section as an instrument prints it`, l IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section as printed has the subsection letter` MEANS elem l (s's `its subsection letters`)

GIVEN s IS A `A section as an instrument prints it`, c IS A `A citation of a section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section as printed has the subsection the citation names` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the subsection letter the citing words name`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST l THEN `the section as printed has the subsection letter` s l

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a section`, s IS A `A section as an instrument prints it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation names the section as printed` MEANS c's `the section the citing words name` EQUALS s's `the section`

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a section`, s IS A `A section as an instrument prints it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citation names a subsection the section has` MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the subsection letter the citing words name`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST l THEN `the section as printed has the subsection letter` s l

GIVEN l IS A `A list of provisions`, p IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the list names the provision` MEANS elem p (l's `the provisions named`)

GIVEN a IS A `A percentage the pages print`, b IS A `A percentage the pages print`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two percentages are equal` MEANS a's `the percentage` EQUALS b's `the percentage`

GIVEN r IS A `A recorded reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS r's `limb (a) holds` AND r's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN r IS A `A recorded reference`
GIVETH A `How a limb was read`
`how limb (a) was read in` MEANS r's `limb (a) was read`

GIVEN r IS A `A recorded reference`
GIVETH A `How a limb was read`
`how limb (b) was read in` MEANS r's `limb (b) was read`
